---
description: Code, comments, and user-facing strings must be written in English only
alwaysApply: true
---

# English only in code

Everything inside source files is written in English:

- Code identifiers, comments, JSDoc
- User-facing text: HTML pages, toasts, button titles, error messages, labels
- Log messages and API error bodies
- `lang` attribute on HTML pages: `lang="en"`

Prefer plain ASCII punctuation in code: `...` not `…`, `-` not `—`, `(` `)` and `:` not full-width `（` `）` `：`.

```js
// BAD
toast('已复制');
// 获取用户信息

// GOOD
toast('Copied');
// fetch user info
```

Exceptions (may contain other languages):

- `README.md` and other docs
- Sample data / fixtures (e.g. `routes/webhook/summary1.json`)
- Values that come from external systems and must match them exactly
